„­bible_version£KJV¤book)§chapter	¨sectionsœ…¤book)§chapter	«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses–„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙvThen he called his twelve disciples together, and gave them power and authority over all devils, and to cure diseases.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙDAnd he sent them to preach the kingdom of God, and to heal the sick.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAnd he said unto them, Take nothing for your journey, neither staves, nor scrip, neither bread, neither money; neither have two coats apiece.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙCAnd whatsoever house ye enter into, there abide, and thence depart.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ…And whosoever will not receive you, when ye go out of that city, shake off the very dust from your feet for a testimony against them.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ]And they departed, and went through the towns, preaching the gospel, and healing every where.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book)§chapter	«first_verseªlast_verse	¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ”Now Herod the tetrarch heard of all that was done by him: and he was perplexed, because that it was said of some, that John was risen from the dead;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙband of some, that Elias had appeared; and of others, that one of the old prophets was risen again.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse	¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙmAnd Herod said, John have I beheaded: but who is this, of whom I hear such things? And he desired to see him.¦layout ªlast_verse	…¤book)§chapter	«first_verse
