„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ›And the people, when they knew it, followed him: and he received them, and spake unto them of the kingdom of God, and healed them that had need of healing.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙßAnd when the day began to wear away, then came the twelve, and said unto him, Send the multitude away, that they may go into the towns and country round about, and lodge, and get victuals: for we are here in a desert place.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ But he said unto them, Give ye them to eat. And they said, We have no more but five loaves and two fishes; except we should go and buy meat for all this people.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙpFor they were about five thousand men. And he said to his disciples, Make them sit down by fifties in a company.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ,And they did so, and made them all sit down.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙThen he took the five loaves and the two fishes, and looking up to heaven, he blessed them, and brake, and gave to the disciples to set before the multitude.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙpAnd they did eat, and were all filled: and there was taken up of fragments that remained to them twelve baskets.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book)§chapter	«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ„And it came to pass, as he was alone praying, his disciples were with him: and he asked them, saying, Whom say the people that I am?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙxThey answering said, John the Baptist; but some say, Elias; and others say, that one of the old prophets is risen again.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙVHe said unto them, But whom say ye that I am? Peter answering said, The Christ of God.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙKAnd he straitly charged them, and commanded them to tell no man that thing;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ—saying, The Son of man must suffer many things, and be rejected of the elders and chief priests and scribes, and be slain, and be raised the third day.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book)§chapter	«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙyAnd he said to them all, If any man will come after me, let him deny himself, and take up his cross daily, and follow me.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙuFor whosoever will save his life shall lose it: but whosoever will lose his life for my sake, the same shall save it.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ\For what is a man advantaged, if he gain the whole world, and lose himself, or be cast away?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¯For whosoever shall be ashamed of me and of my words, of him shall the Son of man be ashamed, when he shall come in his own glory, and in his Father's, and of the holy angels.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙyBut I tell you of a truth, there be some standing here, which shall not taste of death, till they see the kingdom of God.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book)§chapter	«first_verseªlast_verse$¦verses™„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙƒAnd it came to pass about an eight days after these sayings, he took Peter and John and James, and went up into a mountain to pray.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙgAnd as he prayed, the fashion of his countenance was altered, and his raiment was white and glistering.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙGAnd, behold, there talked with him two men, which were Moses and Elias:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙXwho appeared in glory, and spake of his decease which he should accomplish at Jerusalem.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙBut Peter and they that were with him were heavy with sleep: and when they were awake, they saw his glory, and the two men that stood with him.¦layout ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙİAnd it came to pass, as they departed from him, Peter said unto Jesus, Master, it is good for us to be here: and let us make three tabernacles; one for thee, and one for Moses, and one for Elias: not knowing what he said.¦layout ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙoWhile he thus spake, there came a cloud, and overshadowed them: and they feared as they entered into the cloud.¦layout ªlast_verse"„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙRAnd there came a voice out of the cloud, saying, This is my beloved Son: hear him.¦layout ªlast_verse#„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ’And when the voice was past, Jesus was found alone. And they kept it close, and told no man in those days any of those things which they had seen.¦layout ªlast_verse$…¤book)§chapter	«first_verse%ªlast_verse*¦verses–„¥verse%¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙgAnd it came to pass, that on the next day, when they were come down from the hill, much people met him.¦layout ªlast_verse%„¥verse&¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙyAnd, behold, a man of the company cried out, saying, Master, I beseech thee, look upon my son: for he is mine only child.¦layout ªlast_verse&„¥verse'¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAnd, lo, a spirit taketh him, and he suddenly crieth out; and it teareth him that he foameth again, and bruising him hardly departeth from him.¦layout ªlast_verse'„¥verse(¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAAnd I besought thy disciples to cast him out; and they could not.¦layout ªlast_verse(„¥verse)¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‚And Jesus answering said, O faithless and perverse generation, how long shall I be with you, and suffer you? Bring thy son hither.¦layout ªlast_verse)„¥verse*¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¦And as he was yet a coming, the devil threw him down, and tare him. And Jesus rebuked the unclean spirit, and healed the child, and delivered him again to his father.¦layout ªlast_verse*…¤book)§chapter	«first_verse+ªlast_verse-¦verses“„¥verse+¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‘And they were all amazed at the mighty power of God. But while they wondered every one at all things which Jesus did, he said unto his disciples,¦layout ªlast_verse+„¥verse,¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙhLet these sayings sink down into your ears: for the Son of man shall be delivered into the hands of men.¦layout ªlast_verse,„¥verse-¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ…But they understood not this saying, and it was hid from them, that they perceived it not: and they feared to ask him of that saying.¦layout ªlast_verse-…¤book)§chapter	«first_verse.ªlast_verse0¦verses“„¥verse.¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙJThen there arose a reasoning among them, which of them should be greatest.¦layout ªlast_verse.„¥verse/¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙSAnd Jesus, perceiving the thought of their heart, took a child, and set him by him,¦layout ªlast_verse/„¥verse0¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÇand said unto them, Whosoever shall receive this child in my name receiveth me: and whosoever shall receive me receiveth him that sent me: for he that is least among you all, the same shall be great.¦layout ªlast_verse0…¤book)§chapter	«first_verse1ªlast_verse2¦verses’„¥verse1¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙƒAnd John answered and said, Master, we saw one casting out devils in thy name; and we forbad him, because he followeth not with us.¦layout ªlast_verse1„¥verse2¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙQAnd Jesus said unto him, Forbid him not: for he that is not against us is for us.¦layout ªlast_verse2…¤book)§chapter	«first_verse3ªlast_verse8¦verses–„¥verse3¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙyAnd it came to pass, when the time was come that he should be received up, he stedfastly set his face to go to Jerusalem,¦layout ªlast_verse3„¥verse4¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙxand sent messengers before his face: and they went, and entered into a village of the Samaritans, to make ready for him.¦layout ªlast_verse4„¥verse5¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙVAnd they did not receive him, because his face was as though he would go to Jerusalem.¦layout ªlast_verse5„¥verse6¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAnd when his disciples James and John saw this, they said, Lord, wilt thou that we command fire to come down from heaven, and consume them, even as Elias did?¦layout ªlast_verse6„¥verse7¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙWBut he turned, and rebuked them, and said, Ye know not what manner of spirit ye are of.¦layout ªlast_verse7„¥verse8¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙjFor the Son of man is not come to destroy men's lives, but to save them. And they went to another village.¦layout ªlast_verse8…¤book)§chapter	«first_verse9ªlast_verse>¦verses–„¥verse9¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙƒAnd it came to pass, that, as they went in the way, a certain man said unto him, Lord, I will follow thee whithersoever thou goest.¦layout ªlast_verse9„¥verse:¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ~And Jesus said unto him, Foxes have holes, and birds of the air have nests; but the Son of man hath not where to lay his head.¦layout ªlast_verse:„¥verse;¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙaAnd he said unto another, Follow me. But he said, Lord, suffer me first to go and bury my father.¦layout ªlast_verse;„¥verse<¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ]Jesus said unto him, Let the dead bury their dead: but go thou and preach the kingdom of God.¦layout ªlast_verse<„¥verse=¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙvAnd another also said, Lord, I will follow thee; but let me first go bid them farewell, which are at home at my house.¦layout ªlast_verse=„¥verse>¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙtAnd Jesus said unto him, No man, having put his hand to the plough, and looking back, is fit for the kingdom of God.¦layout ªlast_verse>